# --- every remaining BlockPos field on a packet, mutable so the reflective conversion can write it ---
#
# Both packet hooks convert a packet by walking its BlockPos fields and setting them in place, and every one of
# these fields is final. Reflection cannot write a final field, so a packet whose field is not made mutable here
# throws IllegalAccessException the moment it is sent - and the whole packet is dropped. That is not theoretical:
# ClientboundOpenSignEditorPacket failed this way, so the sign editor never opened, and the error only appeared in
# the log as the vanilla handler suppressing it.
